From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:31:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PS5-ECAM's Switch side: the update and DLC files its library
 gave the game, wherever they are

PS5-ECAM's library reads every Switch file's title ID with the keys, in any folder of its games
folder, and shows a game's update and DLC on its page. Eden took them only from the game files
folder's updates/ and dlc/, the game's own folder, and the files beside the game: an update in a
folder other than the game's (Games/ and Updates/ side by side, one at the top while the game is in a
folder) showed on the game's page and the game ran without it (PS5-ECAM issue 106). Copying it to the
PS5's updates/ was the only way.

- --set addon_files: the files PS5-ECAM gave the game, absolute paths with a '|' between them
  (game_addons.h's ListedFiles: NSP and XCI only, each once, at most 64).
- They go to the ExternalContentProvider as the files beside the game do, for the game PS5-ECAM asked
  for alone (a game it starts itself gets none), and the log says how many opened.
---
 headless/game_addons.h    | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 headless/main.cpp         | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 headless/settings_store.h |  5 +++++
 3 files changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/headless/game_addons.h b/headless/game_addons.h
index 18db0f1..5f7b947 100644
--- a/headless/game_addons.h
+++ b/headless/game_addons.h
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 //     which decides without opening the file; one whose name gives none is opened to read what it
 //     holds (main.cpp). Another game's files are neither handed to Eden nor kept open.
 // dlc/ in the game files folder is read as updates/ is: the other systems' folders have one.
+// And the files PS5-ECAM's Switch side gave the game itself, wherever they are (ListedFiles).
 #pragma once
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cctype>
@@ -88,4 +89,22 @@ inline void Beside(const std::filesystem::path& rom, std::uint64_t base, std::ve
     }
 }
 
+// The update and DLC files PS5-ECAM's Switch side gave the game (--set addon_files): its library reads
+// each file's title ID with the keys, in any folder of its games folder, and shows them on the game's
+// page; one in a folder other than the game's (Games/ and Updates/ side by side) was never applied
+// (PS5-ECAM issue 106). Absolute paths of NSP and XCI files with a '|' between them (FAT and exFAT
+// names cannot have one), each once; at most 64, each under 1024 characters. Anything else is left out.
+inline std::vector<std::string> ListedFiles(std::string_view text) {
+    std::vector<std::string> files;
+    for (size_t at = 0; at <= text.size() && files.size() < 64;) {
+        const size_t bar = std::min(text.find('|', at), text.size());
+        const std::string_view piece = text.substr(at, bar - at);
+        if (piece.size() > 1 && piece.size() < 1024 && piece.front() == '/' && IsSwitchFile(std::filesystem::path{piece}) &&
+            std::find(files.begin(), files.end(), piece) == files.end())
+            files.emplace_back(piece);
+        at = bar + 1;
+    }
+    return files;
+}
+
 }  // namespace Eden::AddOns
diff --git a/headless/main.cpp b/headless/main.cpp
index 54d0916..6c21094 100644
--- a/headless/main.cpp
+++ b/headless/main.cpp
@@ -718,6 +718,8 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
         }
         std::string forwarded_game;
         bool forwarded_session = false;
+        // the forwarded game's file: the update and DLC files PS5-ECAM gave are for it alone
+        std::string listed_for;
         if (!forwarded.rom.empty() && (last_crash.report.empty() || ecam_started)) {
             const std::string path = Eden::ResolveForwardedRom(forwarded.rom, Eden::AssetsPath("roms"));
             if (!path.empty() && Eden::FileExists(path)) forwarded_game = path;
@@ -800,6 +802,7 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
             guest_fault_retries = 0;
             forwarded_session = true;
             selected_game = std::exchange(forwarded_game, {});
+            listed_for = selected_game;
             Eden::BootTrace::Line("starting the forwarded game");
             KeepForwardedCover(selected_game);
 #ifdef EDEN_ECAM
@@ -1880,6 +1883,23 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
                     }
                 }
 #endif
+                // The update and DLC files PS5-ECAM's Switch side gave the game, wherever in its games
+                // folder they are (game_addons.h's ListedFiles): its library showed them on the game's
+                // page, so the game runs with them. Those of the game it asked for alone.
+                if (game && guest && !listed_for.empty() && selected_game == listed_for &&
+                    !Eden::Session().addon_files.empty()) {
+                    std::vector<FileSys::VirtualFile> listed;
+                    for (const std::string& path : Eden::Session().addon_files)
+                        if (path != selected_game)
+                            if (auto file = system.GetFilesystem()->OpenFile(path, FileSys::OpenMode::Read))
+                                listed.push_back(std::move(file));
+                    Eden::Report("launch", ("Update and DLC PS5-ECAM gave the game: " + std::to_string(listed.size()) + " of " +
+                                            std::to_string(Eden::Session().addon_files.size()) + " files opened").c_str());
+                    if (auto* external = system.GetFileSystemController().GetExternalContentProvider();
+                        external && !listed.empty())
+                        external->AddDirectory(std::make_shared<FileSys::VectorVfsDirectory>(
+                            std::move(listed), std::vector<FileSys::VirtualDir>{}, "PS5-ECAM's"));
+                }
                 // The game's own contents, registered as Eden's desktop frontends do before booting a
                 // game (ConfigureFilesystemProvider). An update's data is a patch on the base game's:
                 // the patch manager looks the base up here, and without it applied only the update's
